# Paths removed from Android-x86's system image before it is published
# (scripts/prepare-image.sh, scripts/slim-system.py).  One absolute path
# inside the image per line; directories go with everything in them.  A path
# the image does not have is skipped, so alternative names can be listed.
#
# Google's apps (the ISO inherits vendor/google/products/gms.mk).  None of
# them is needed to boot, and Play services is the most expensive package
# of a first boot.  Their permission and sysconfig XML files under /etc are
# left alone: entries for packages that are not installed are ignored.
/priv-app/PrebuiltGmsCore
/priv-app/GmsCore
/priv-app/GmsCoreSetupPrebuilt
/priv-app/Phonesky
/priv-app/Vending
/priv-app/GoogleServicesFramework
/priv-app/GoogleLoginService
/priv-app/GoogleBackupTransport
/priv-app/GoogleFeedback
/priv-app/GoogleOneTimeInitializer
/priv-app/GooglePartnerSetup
/priv-app/AndroidPlatformServices
/priv-app/ConfigUpdater
/app/GoogleContactsSyncAdapter
/app/GoogleCalendarSyncAdapter
/priv-app/GoogleContactsSyncAdapter
